In article <15097@plains.NoDak.edu>, you write:
 > I am currently in the middle of a game in nethack.  I have made it to a sixth
 > level barbarian.  I found guantlets of power on the third level, a ring of
 > increased power on the fourth level, a pick ax on the fifth level, and was
 > saying to myself this is really going to be a good game.  Then I got to the   
 > sixth level and I steped onto a pile of gold, probably about 150 pieces.  The
 > next thing I know, I am a gnome wizard.  Instead of xp, I now have HD.  I have
 > only 16 hitpoints rather than 70.  I remember fighting two were-creatures, but
 > I killed them both before they were able to inflict any damage on me.  I
 > checked the square the best I know how, but I couldn't find any traps there.
 > Does ANYBODY know what happened?  How can I get back to my normal barbarian 
 > character?  HELP!!!!!!!
 > Thanks in advance,
 > George Grabrick

Seems that you stepped on a polymorph trap.  They sometimes disappear after use.
There are many ways to return to your normal barbarian:
1. Quaff some holy water.
2. Pray
3. Just keep playing.  The gnome wizard will time out.
4. Polymorph yourself with a wand.
5. Get hit badly, so that the gnome wizard looses all his hitpoints. You will
   then return to human form, with some hit points missing.  Be sure that you can
   kill or get away from the monster afterwards...

